        <headline>Small Craft Advisory issued September 24 at 2:20PM EDT until September 25 at 4:00PM EDT by NWS Baltimore MD/Washington DC</headline>
        <description>* WHAT...For the Small Craft Advisory, north winds 15 to 25 kt
with gusts up to 30 kt and waves 2 to 4 ft. For the Gale
Watch, north winds 20 to 30 kt with gusts up to 35 kt and
waves 2 to 5 ft possible.

* WHERE...Chesapeake Bay from North Beach MD to Smith Point VA,
Tidal Potomac from Cobb Island MD to Smith Point VA, and
Tangier Sound and the inland waters surrounding Bloodsworth
Island.

* WHEN...For the Small Craft Advisory, until 4 PM EDT Friday.
For the Gale Watch, from Friday afternoon through Saturday
afternoon.

* IMPACTS...Strong winds can cause hazardous waves which could
capsize or damage vessels.
</description>
        <instruction>Mariners should consider altering plans to avoid possible
hazardous conditions.  Remain in port, seek safe harbor, alter
course, and/or secure the vessel for hazardous wind and waves.</instruction>
